  "term": "institutional review board",
  "definition": "An institutional review board is an independent committee set up by an organization to protect the rights, safety, and well-being of people taking part in biomedical or behavioral research. It reviews research plans, changes to those plans, and the informed consent process on an ongoing basis.",
